  "step_2": "The individual considers two aspects: (1) the potential to win 100 Euros more with Lottery A (2500 vs 2400), and (2) the fact that Lottery A has only 1 percentage point lower chance of winning (33% vs 34%) compared to Lottery B. The justification for choosing Lottery A is based on the higher potential gain despite a slightly lower probability of winning. The individual does not mention any reference point or aspiration level derived from averaging outcomes, nor do they refer to comparing outcomes relative to such a benchmark. There is no indication that outcomes were evaluated based on their deviation from a computed aspiration level.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (ignoring probabilities) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. The relevant information—such as the aspiration level of ~1633.33 and the comparison of probabilities of positive deviations (33% for A, 34% for B)—is not reflected in the verbal report. Instead, the individual focuses on the absolute difference in outcomes (100 Euros) and the small difference in winning probabilities. The justification is based on a trade-off between higher gain and slightly lower chance, not on deviations from an aspiration level. Therefore, the cognitive process described in the verbal report does not align with the decision reason. There is no evidence that the individual computed or used an aspiration level or evaluated outcomes based on whether they exceed it.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
