  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes, then evaluating which lottery has a higher chance of exceeding this level. The aspiration level (-2250) and the comparison of probabilities of positive deviations from it are not mentioned or implied in the verbal report. The individual instead focuses solely on the maximum possible loss and its magnitude, preferring B because -3000 is half of -6000. This reasoning aligns more with minimax or loss-aversion heuristics rather than the aspiration-level rule based on mean outcomes. There is no evidence that the individual calculated or used the mean of outcomes or assessed differences from a central reference point. The justification is based on outcome severity, not deviation from an average. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
